Preserve the computation the reader should perform.

⸻

Final Compression

The original claim:

“Optimize for equivalent reasoning.”

becomes something like:

Separate the costume.
Recover the operator.
Render a new costume that preserves the operator.

Or even more compactly:

Surface changes.
Function survives.
Re-render deliberately.

That, I think, is the deepest reusable primitive here. It also explains why metaphors, algorithms, diagrams, equations, stories, and code can all be valuable for the same underlying idea: each is a different rendering optimized for a different set of constraints, while aiming to preserve the task-relevant structure rather than the exact form.